From: Ghaf contributors <ghaf@tii.ae>
Subject: [PATCH] nvkms: force no-syncpt support for display-only guests

Without a physical host1x assigned to the display-only VM,
pDevEvo->supportsSyncpts must be false or NVKMS's mandatory per-window
post-syncpoint allocation fails. Force the no-syncpt path so the software
compositor drives display with CPU buffers and no explicit fences.
---
diff --git a/nvdisplay/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c b/nvdisplay/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c
--- a/nvdisplay/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c
+++ b/nvdisplay/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c
@@ -101,6 +101,8 @@
 
 NvBool nvkms_kernel_supports_syncpts(void)
 {
+    /* disp-vm has no physical host1x syncpoints. */
+    return NV_FALSE;
 /*
  * Note this only checks that the kernel has the prerequisite
  * support for syncpts; callers must also check that the hardware
